.TH "LMM" "1" "Jul 2026" "lmm 1.24.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-search - Search for mods


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm search <query> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Search for mods in the configured sources.

.PP
If --source is not specified, all configured sources for the game are
searched concurrently and the results are merged. Results already
installed in the target profile (-p/--profile, default: active profile)
are marked [installed].

.PP
Use --category and --tag to filter results; support varies by source.
--category is honored by NexusMods and CurseForge; --tag is currently
NexusMods only. Custom sources (directory/manifest/API) ignore both.
The values each source accepts are source-specific.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm search skyui --game skyrim-se
  lmm search "immersive armor" --game skyrim-se --source nexusmods
  lmm search "armor" --game skyrim-se --category armor --tag lore-friendly
  lmm search "armor" --game skyrim-se --profile survival


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--category\fP=""
	filter by category (source-specific ID or name)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for search

.PP
\fB-l\fP, \fB--limit\fP=10
	maximum number of results

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to check for installed mods (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--source\fP=""
	mod source to search (default: all configured sources)

.PP
\fB--tag\fP=[]
	filter by tag (repeatable; source-specific)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output in JSON format (list, status, search, update, conflicts, verify, mod show, source list)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


